# Fetched from upstream by fetch.py — third-party files under a different
# licence, and the netlist alone is 12 MB (larger than src/sqlite3.c, this
# repo's biggest file).  Provenance and digests live in fetch.py.
ariane.v
fakeram45_256x16.lef
# The technology LEF carries a PROPRIETARY Nangate header — "you are not
# permitted to use the Marks without prior written consent" — so it is
# fetched and never vendored, which is the same treatment the other two get
# for a milder reason.
NangateOpenCellLibrary.tech.lef
*.part
*.bdb

# Flow outputs — regenerated by `bin/buda flow/ariane133/ariane133.buda`.
out/
log/

# pdngen output — generated by `openroad -exit flow/ariane133/pdn.tcl`
# (docs/internal/openroad_pdn_recipe.md).  Megabytes of our own generated
# artifact; digest-pinning a file we generate proves nothing about whether
# it is right (recipe §7).  Regenerate it, do not commit it.
ariane_pdn.def

# …and the spliced DEF derived from it — `demo/ariane/ariane.def` carrying
# that PDN's SPECIALNETS, which is what `ariane133_ndr_straps.buda` imports
# (its `require_file` states how to rebuild it).  Generated from a generated
# file, so the same rule applies twice over.
ariane_keepout.def

# The build trace `btcl -i` writes beside a live checkpoint (its name is
# `<ckpt>.trace`, so the `*.bdb` rule above does not reach it).
*.bdb.trace
